# binary:
# The binary naturals: binary_zero, binary_even h for 2h and binary_odd h for
# 2h + 1, each a term of three cases, the low bit outermost, and the
# library's binary arithmetic: the lambdalattice files of the directory
# binary/. binary is the contract of the canonical numerals: the even case
# excludes zero below it, so a member has no leading zero bit. binary_set P
# is their type as a set of constructor shapes, P true for the canonical
# naturals and false for the canonical positive ones, which is what a filter
# `x ∥ binary_set true` decodes at. The backend's facts are binary_prolog_backend's. A number
# literal's value is integer/from_cbor's.
#
# NOT HERE: the functions a set-free point writes for itself (the rebuild,
# the complement, the unit law's step; corpora/contest_set_free_premises.pl).
# A point writes them so that recognising a library function does not answer
# it, and a file in this directory would give them an address.
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ
    . fixpoint
    λ self n
    . n binary_zero (λh. self h top (λg. binary_even λ. binary_even g) λk. binary_even λ. binary_odd k) λl. binary_odd λ. self l
  )
λ binary
# binary_set:
# The canonical binary naturals as a set of constructor shapes, one set per
# boolean p: at true, zero, 2h for a positive h and 2h + 1 for any h; at
# false, the positive ones alone, 2h for a positive h and 2h + 1 for any h.
# So binary_even binary_zero, whose field is read at false, is in neither.
# The shapes are the constructors' bodies, as nat_type writes them.
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ
    . fixpoint λself p. ((λh z e o. o h) λ. self true + (λh z e o. e h) λ. self false + p (λz e o. z) top)
  )
λ binary_set
. export binary_zero binary_even binary_odd binary binary_set
